cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vibrotrack in academic work, please cite this repository."
title: "vibrotrack: dense particle tracking for quasi-2D vibrated granular monolayers"
abstract: >-
  A command-line toolkit that turns high-speed TIFF frames of a quasi-2D vibrated
  granular monolayer into a hash-checked particle dataset: centres, radii,
  orientations, track ids, a geometry product, and batch-level admission gates.
authors:
  - name: "Diraw"
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-11-12"
url: "https://github.com/Diraw/vibrotrack"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Diraw/vibrotrack"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - granular materials
  - particle tracking
  - computer vision
  - vibration
